First the bug:

	As I was on my way up the dungeon (on my way to my very first
_ascension_) Entire portions of the dungeon began mapping themselves
out for me. Passages and wals that were out of my line of site would
suddenly magically appear. It was like I had the intrinsic automatic
magic mapping. I was very much afraid that this would crash my game
before I could finish my very first _ascension_, but the game stayed
in one piece and I was able to _ascend_ for the very first time.
	This newfound ability actually aided my very first _ascension_
by causing the air portal to appear some ten spaces away. It was as if
some one had crossed telepathy with automatic searching.
	Question: is this a bug that others have run into?

Now the discovery:
	Apparently the Dev team was thinking ahead when they
programmed the astral level. I put on a towel, and identified (using
"/") various '@' characters. I found a priest of Okam-whosis and
headed in that direction only to discover that he was a blasphemous
priest of Okam-whosis (I have forgotten the exact words) serving the
neutral God.
	Needless to say, I killed him, found the real temple of
Okam-whosis (which was in the temple left) and _ascended_ for the very
first time!

